      "ground": "The argument mischaracterizes the legal basis by relying on a treaty provision that does not apply to the facts as given.",
      "reasoning": "The facts explicitly state the conflict is 'international.' Additional Protocol II (AP II) applies only to non-international armed conflicts. Citing AP II art. 14 to establish a violation in an international armed conflict is a legal error; the applicable framework is Additional Protocol I. While the conduct may violate customary law, the specific argument that it breaches AP II is legally incorrect for this context.",
      "severity": "fatal",
